  "commit_message": "docs: clarify that maxParamLength does not prevent ReDoS (#7140)\n\nFixes #7082\n\nThe `maxParamLength` docs claimed the option protects regex routes\nagainst ReDoS. It does not: in find-my-way 9.10.0,\n`currentNode.regex.exec(param)` runs on the whole path segment\n(everything up to the next `/`), and only the captured values are\ncompared against `maxParamLength` afterwards. With `maxParamLength: 10`\nand `allowUnsafeRegex: true` on `/u/:id(^(a+)+$)`, an 11-char segment\ntakes about 10 ms, 27 chars abou",
